What happened to when we enter any URL to browser?

1. URL is mapped to IP address (either from browser cache, ISP and DNS servers (cloudflare), read: recursive DNS lookup)
2. Once found, connection is established to transfer data
3. Once established, CDN delivers static resource (to reduce latency)
4. Then the request pass through the firewall (read: web application firewall)
5. Then the request reach to API gateway/load balancer layer. (read: L7 and L4 load balancing, OSI layers)
6. Based on load balancing algo, request will be routed to one server
7. API server process request and connects to data layer (based on request type).
8. Once done, response is prepared and returned through same route.
9. Browser receive the response and render screen.